-- VHF records joined to county boundaries, for the county maps.
-- Boundaries from kenya-county-boundaries.sql; records from the precomputed line list
-- (nphiis_vhf_line_list). Not precomputed: the Jinja below applies the dashboard filters
-- before the join, so counties with no matching records still draw.
SELECT b.county_key, b.county_name, b.boundary AS `County Boundary`, v.*
FROM (
-- Kenya county boundaries for Superset deck.gl polygon maps.
--
-- Source: geoBoundaries KEN ADM1 (gbOpen, simplified), from RCMRD GeoPortal,
-- public domain. https://www.geoboundaries.org
-- Each county keeps its largest part's outer ring (deck.gl's polygon layer
-- takes one ring per row), simplified with Douglas-Peucker at 0.01 degrees and
-- rounded to 3 decimals. Coordinates are [longitude, latitude].
--
-- Join on county_key, the county name in capitals with anything but A-Z
-- removed, so "Tharaka-Nithi", "THARAKA NITHI" and "Murang'a" all match.
-- county_name is the HAPI county Location name.
--
-- Written as (VALUES ...) AS t(...), which both Spark and Postgres accept.
